    stylePrompt: "Glam metal commercial track, 128 BPM. Heavy screeching lead guitar with feedback, dive bombs and big bends in the style of late-80s glam metal, distorted power chords, big gated drums, anthemic gang vocals chanting \"GLAM-SHAM-POO\". Neon synth stabs sit underneath the guitars for a little commercial shine but the guitars stay dominant. Sudden angry Japanese salaryman shouting samples for comedy. College-party energy mixed with corporate chaos. Female vocals: one dry and slightly raspy (Rubella), one brighter and more chaotic (Lillith). High-energy, over-the-top, slightly unhinged joke TV commercial for a shampoo that is way too loud. Structure: guitar-screech intro, verse, pre-chorus with shouting samples, big chorus, verse 2 trade, short bridge, final bigger chorus, feedback outro.",
    lyrics: "[Intro – 8 bars]\n(Screeching guitar feedback → big chord)\nKenji (spoken, hyped):\n\"Konichiwa... from the neon temples of Glamora!\"\n\n[Verse 1]\nHair so loud it headbangs alone\nSplit ends screaming like a power chord\nOne wash and the volume’s gone\nFrom quiet to ordinance war\n(Glam-Sham-Poo College class of loud)\n\n[Pre-Chorus]\n(Businessmen shouting samples layered under the guitars)\n\"This is not in the budget!\"\n\"売上目標未達!!\"\n\"Who approved this formula?!\"\n\n[Chorus]\nGLAM-SHAM-POO!\nMake it SCREECH!\nVolume so high the elevator freaks\nGLAM-SHAM-POO!\nRock your scalp!\nClean hair, loud life, no regrets\n\n[Verse 2 – Rubella + Lillith trade]\nLillith: I poured it in the neon signs\nNow every tube screams on key\nRubella: HOA came with a fine\nMy hair out-screeched the citation fee\n\n[Bridge – Office Argument]\n(Guitars thin out for a second, fluorescent tension)\nSalaryman 1: This product is chaos!\nSalaryman 2: The numbers are bleeding!\nKenji (still hyped): But the hair… is succeeding!\nAll: GLAM! SHAM! POO!\n\n[Final Chorus – bigger, more gang vocals + guitar scream]\nGLAM-SHAM-POO!\nMake it SCREECH!\nVolume so high the elevator freaks\nGLAM-SHAM-POO!\nRock your scalp!\nResults may attract laser snakes\n\n[Outro]\n(Guitar feedback + fluorescent hum)\nKenji: Available in your building’s vending machine…\n(fading salaryman yell) “経費削減!!”",
    notes: "Glam metal first, commercial polish second. 126–132 BPM, key E minor or A major.\n\n**Bed lock (2026-09-05):** the picture is cut against **Ultra Screech 2 with the take-1 opening scream spliced on** — `Ultra_Screech_2_with_scream.mp3`, ~2:51 at 128 BPM. The old 1:45–2:10 target is retired; the stills package was re-timed to ten segments rather than stretched. Audio stays out of the repo (external hosting, keep the clone light).\n\nVocal split: Rubella = dry, slightly raspy, exhausted cabaret (already tired of this commercial). Lillith = brighter, chaotic, fully committed. Gang vocals on “GLAM-SHAM-POO!” Kenji spoken hype intercut as salesman energy.\n\nStills-first package: original 5-still commercial (`glam_sham_poo_commercial_clip.mp4`) is the preferred visual. Spoken commercial audio stays scratch until the Minimax track drops under those stills.\n\nLipsync: beat-sync over mouth shapes. On-camera mouths only for the gang title chant. Verses are performance / attitude. Hold the product bottle on chorus 1 and the logo end card on the final chorus.\n\nJoke-commercial energy: pretend confusion, over-commitment, network accidentally approved something far too loud. Humor is glam-metal sincerity selling shampoo — the deliberate opposite of the glossy dance-pop a real cosmetic brand would buy.\n\nPreferred stills spine (original commercial): Kenji hero pitch → laundry-room dual frontwomen → product bottle → big glam energy → logo end card. Intercut fluorescent office only on salaryman samples. Keep glam volume up — big teased hair, not cartoon beehives; the hair-dialed-back redo is not primary and the v2 office sequence is an alternate.\n\nThe 2:51 conform adds a cold-open scream, a Verse 2 neon-pour / HOA-citation trade, a handbook §12 macro on the second pre-chorus, and a bridge-plus-solo block before the logo takes the final chorus.\n\nTimed Suggestions segments live in `src/data/songCutaways.ts` (`mv-ultra-screech`). Copy-ready stills prompts: `prompts/glam-sham-poo-segments.md`. Concept, spoken-VO script, and product lore: `ideas/glam-sham-poo-commercial.md`.\n\n*Updated 2026-09-05 — bed locked to Ultra Screech 2 with the take-1 scream (~2:51); stills package re-timed to ten segments. Glam metal first. College lore + stills-first package.*",
    instrumental: false,
