    title: "Marble Tick Tack",
    genre: "Experimental tick-tock instrumental",
    description: "Pure animation bridge (~2:03). No vocal. Cabinet marble chorus walks a night lot — alley fences, impossible lawn, electromagnet tower, ferrofluid rain — and snaps home. Roley Voss lane.",
    episode: "Musical Cutaway / Visual Experiment",
    stylePrompt: "Instrumental only. No vocal. Tight mechanical tick-tock clockwork as the pulse, dry wood-block and marble-click percussion on the off-beats, sub-bass hits that stand an object up then let it slump in the gap, sparse analog synth grit, no melody hook, no lyric, no choir. Quiet pockets near 0:48 and 1:27. Full engine 0:50–1:20. Decay last three seconds to a single click. About 2:03. Experimental animation-bridge bed, not a song with a singer.",
    lyrics: "[Instrumental — no vocal]\n\n[0:00–0:10 Tick into groove]\nWarm cabinet. Marbles hop in the grooves. Disc stack counter-rotates. One cube slides for the glasses.\n\n[0:10–0:20 Growing]\nTwo spheres stop at the doorway. Empty floor. One-frame jump on the kick. Out onto dirt.\n\n[0:20–0:40 Hits]\nDirt alley. Copper Rodin cyclotron. Disc spinning on the top winding. Big jump gap into gears that never touch.\n\n[0:40–0:50 Build / freeze]\nFence gap. Unreal green. Two spheres a millimeter apart. Freeze at 0:48, dancers included.\n\n[0:50–1:20 Full engine]\nCoils on with the kick. Tower stands, slumps in the gap. Three-phase orbit. Rod pair tumbling end-over-end. Hung ferrofluid appears, still not falling.\n\n[1:20–1:30 Quiet]\nFrozen ferrofluid rain hanging. Tremble only. Millimeter gap. Do not fall yet.\n\n[1:30–2:00 Return]\nRain thaws, smashes, wraps chrome. Bound pair mutual-orbits home past the dry Rodin. Last jump into the Gauss chain on the same shelf.\n\n[2:00–2:03 Decay]\nOne marble. Two magnets a millimeter apart. Disc spinning down. Speakers dead.",
    notes: "Pure animation bridge. Roley Voss owns the lane. No faces, no lips, no building-cast. Station objects hop in place; magnets are the second system and may travel. Track lives locally as `artifacts/marble_tick_tack.mp3` (2:03.06) — not committed yet to keep the clone light. Board: `ideas/marble-tick-tack.md`. Timed Grok Imagine + Gemini Omni prompts: `prompts/marble-tick-tack-segments.md`. Suggestions id: `marble-tick-tack`. Test order: clip 1 cabinet, clip 3 Rodin alley, clip 6 tower, clip 10 rain. Do not generate 2–4 until 1 holds the cabinet.\n\nSibling cutaway on the same bed: **Marble Tick Tack: Wrong Sets** (`ideas/marble-tick-tack-worlds.md`, `prompts/marble-tick-tack-worlds-segments.md`, Suggestions id `marble-tick-tack-worlds`). Night-lot A–M stays the production take. Wrong Sets hops desert / woods / ice / space / London / Seoul with new magnet bodies; magnets never notice.",
    instrumental: true,
