    lyrics: "[Intro — Gavel Rimshot]\n(Horns enter wrong, then lock)\n\n[Verse 1]\nItem three on the emergency agenda\nThe bin is the wrong shade of democratic blue\nI have swatches. I have charts. I have God.\nThe sky can wait its turn.\n\n[Pre-Chorus]\nIt's not a portal\nIt's a cul-de-sac feature\n\n[Chorus]\nIt's the wrong shade of democratic blue\nIt's anarchy blue, Karen, and I won't have it\nIn my cul-de-sac\nWrong shade of democratic blue\nRaise the bin like a battle standard\nWe will die about this (metaphorically)\n(Karen has a form)\n\n[Verse 2]\nA purple light in the driveway\nBrad is power-washing a sigil\nDale gavels through the explosion\nThe gavel is cracked. He calls it character.\n\n[Pre-Chorus]\nIt's not a haunting\nIt's seasonal ambience with liability\n\n[Chorus]\nIt's the wrong shade of democratic blue\nIt's anarchy blue, Karen, and I won't have it\nIn my cul-de-sac\nWrong shade of democratic blue\nRaise the bin like a battle standard\nWe will die about this (metaphorically)\n(Karen has a form)\n\n[Breakdown — Off-Key Trumpet]\n(Single trumpet plays the HOA hold-music “take me home.” Everyone waits. Pizza Guy's doorbell. Nobody comments.)\n\n[Final Chorus]\nIt's the wrong shade of democratic blue\nThe rift can stay if the bin is compliant\nWrong shade of democratic blue\nEveryone sits back down\nAdjusts a name tag\nAs if nothing\nAs if nothing\nAs if nothing happened",
    notes: "HOA episode (Episode 4 / Item Three) musical cutaway or end-credits. Starts petty, escalates into glorious rebellion, ends with everyone calmly sitting down when the pizza guy arrives. Structural flaw: the breakdown trumpet is a whole step flat and nobody corrects it. Visual: seven adults in folding chairs screaming the chorus while a glowing portal spins behind the whiteboard; a recycling bin as a battle standard; final shot everyone sitting, name tags straight. Ready for Minimax. High contrast to the velvet tracks.",
