    lyrics: "[Intro — 8 bars, diegetic / tinny]\n(instrumental; off-balance dryer thump on bar 5, not bar 1)\n\n[Verse 1 — HER]\nThat one's not level\nIt worked in June\n\n[Verse 1 — HIM]\nWe're both available\nThat's worse than alone\n\n[Verse 1 — HER]\nThe light makes everyone processed\nExcept the thump\n\n[Verse 1 — HIM]\nThe thump knows what we're not saying\n\n[Pre-Chorus — HER]\nThe hour goes by anyway\n\n[Pre-Chorus — HIM]\nWe don't have to name it\n\n[Chorus — alternate, unison only on title]\nLaundromat saints\nDon't ask for names\nLaundromat saints\nThe dryer keeps time wrong\nIf the song says it\nWe'll let the buzzer take it back\n\n[Verse 2 — HIM]\nYou came here instead of going home\nI came here instead of calling\n\n[Verse 2 — HER]\nThe corner TV is always on\nNobody watches it on purpose\n\n[Verse 2 — HIM]\nThe mop goes around us\nThat's the whole religion\n\n[Verse 2 — HER]\nSaints don't mean good\nSaints mean showed up\n\n[Pre-Chorus — HER]\nThe hour goes by anyway\n\n[Pre-Chorus — HIM]\nWe don't have to name it\n\n[Chorus]\nLaundromat saints\nDon't ask for names\nLaundromat saints\nThe dryer keeps time wrong\nIf the song says it\nWe'll let the buzzer take it back\n\n[Bridge — instrumental, or one held vowel]\n(piano and dryer thump; this is where the dance is — no words compete with the faces)\n\n[Final Chorus — half volume, as if the TV took it back]\nLaundromat saints\nDon't ask for names\nLaundromat saints\nThe dryer keeps time wrong\nIf the song says it\nWe'll let the buzzer take it back\n\n[Outro — 4 bars, cut off by buzzer]\n(dryer BUZZ — song does not finish; mid-phrase cut is correct)",
    notes: "## Production notes\n- **Episode placement:** Musical cutaway scoring `notes/scenes/laundromat-slow-dance.md` — diegetic on the corner EyeWash TV, then blooms past diegetic. Pairs fluorescents + rain glass + one machine with an opinion.\n- **Voice map:** Anonymous dual presence — alternate lines, never sweet harmony. Rubella-ish + dry baritone or second female. The Laundromat Saints are never credited on screen.\n- **Structural flaw:** Dryer thump on bar 5, not bar 1, for the entire runtime. Do not quantize or \"fix\" in mix.\n- **Sibling track:** Empty Parking Lot Waltz (same waltz DNA, colder / more devastating). Static Between Stations can underscore the liminal drive *into* this room.\n- **Runtime target:** 3:00–3:30. Outro must be buzzer-cuttable.\n- **Continuity Voice:** Optional on the corner TV before diegetic bloom — not required.",
