    notes: "**What the song is**\nA ruin inventory for The Two. The roof has not fallen; it is **waiting**, which is a kind of hospitality. “Finally. Natural ventilation.” is load-bearing and must stay deadpan. Scratchpad hook: *We said we'd leave before the roof came down / Turns out the roof knows how to wait.*\n\nCheap to picture: one ballroom, one hole, two glasses, berries, plaster.\n\n**Craft (keep this off-mic)**\n- *Neon Exit Sign* owns mascara and the burning-town walk. This is **the ceiling**, not the road.\n- *Empty Parking Lot Waltz* owns aftermath in a lot. This is aftermath that is still a room.\n- *The Pour* owns hired climate (foundry). Do not import molten iron.\n- *House of Mirrors Rally* owns the ping-pong metronome and the mascara beat. Do not score the rally. No paddles.\n- Do not belt “wait.” Do not make the extra bar a joke fill.\n\n**Production notes**\n- **Episode placement:** Standalone musical cutaway; visual cousin to the abandoned ballroom in `notes/scenes/house-of-mirrors-rally.md` without replacing that scene’s bed. The Two as silhouettes or red-lip close-ups, not named on screen.\n- **Voice:** Rubella. Optional Lillith room-echo on last “wait” only.\n- **Structural flaw:** Extra bar after every verse (and the bridge). Piano late into the next section. Never corrected.\n- **Runtime target:** 2:00–2:20.",
